write,likeread,cantransferlessdatathanwasrequested,accordingtothefollowing
rules for the return value:
• If the value equalscount, the requested number of bytes has been transferred.
• If the value is positive, but smaller than count, only part of the data has been
transferred. The program will most likely retry writing the rest of the data.
• Ifthevalueis0,nothingwaswritten.Thisresultisnotanerror,andthereisno
reasontoreturnanerrorcode.Onceagain,thestandardlibraryretriesthecallto
